A||N||3||Seanh||Rear brake pad retainer clips, I don't have?||||1||
Z||000000||Seanh||04-25-2001||09:44 PM||||I have my calipers all rebuilt and all, I am ready to install. I am putting the inner pad on, and it says there should be a retainer clip that hooks to the pad and the caliper piston. One of my calipers had been replaced by the previous owner, so its newer then the other. The older one does have provisions on the piston for the clip, but when I took the pad off there was no clip on there. The newer one doesn't even have a place for the clip on the piston. So whats the deal? Apperently you don't need the clip after all? My pads have the "D" shaped notches on them to fit into the piston, but thats about all. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||ICAL||04-25-2001||10:26 PM||||I don't beleive my car had them either but I purchased them from the dealer for 5.70 each. The part number is 018011729 and they call them a spring. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-26-2001||07:38 PM||||The clip is allot more important than most people tell you. It is NOT just to stop the pad rattling.<P>The clip pulls the pad off the rotor reducing drag and wear. It also keeps the lock pins on the pad engaged in the piston face. Those pins prevent the piston from rotating.<P>One of my calipers is "notch free as well." There are aparently 2 versions of the pistons. As yet I can't find out if there are 2 versions of clip. I took the regular clip and carefully pryed it into the piston boot groove. (It's been like that for 30,000 miles. actually works better than the other one with the notches.)<P>I plan on rebuilding the calipers over the summer. (I suspect a developing E brake problem...) I'm going to, hopefully, use the GM rebuild kit from the V6 recall. That is suposed to have diferant pistons and all the other parts.... we'll see then I guess.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||04-30-2001||10:16 AM||||I have some clips if you want them. They were in the kit I used to rebuild my front calipers.<P>E-Mail me and I'll send them to you.||||reg||1
